 "reading": "R58.4 against the lens (d475806, built again in a scratch worktree and served on its own port), three runs each, interleaved in one lock hold per size. 1512x982@2: renderer compositor [272, 271, 270] against [237, 241, 243] ms, display compositor [174, 175, 175] against [157, 161, 162]; 1920x1080@1: [254, 291, 253] against [293, 291, 292], [162, 182, 162] against [189, 186, 188]. The limits are 450 and 300: PASS at both sizes. At 1512x982@2 the new build is about 30 ms more on the renderer compositor and 12 to 14 ms more on the display one than the lens (the first round's R58.1 was 5 to 14 and 2 to 6): probably because the early tiles are now 0.0125 apart, so the map's picture changes source in nearly every frame of the first 0.15 s, where it changed every second or third frame before (not separated out by a run of its own). At 1920x1080@1 the base set ran at a load of 2.7 to 3.1 and the R58.4 set at 2.2 to 2.4, so the two sets are not on equal ground (the base is the slower of them there); the rows carry each run's load. Every run of both builds has exactly one dropped frame, in the change's first frame (R125, R127: the tool exempts only the earliest dropped frame and only within 50 ms of the start mark); none after it.",
